  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Protection of Vulnerable Conflict-Affected Population</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the full-scale invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation on 24 February 2022, the humanitarian situation in the country has quickly deteriorated. Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to the protection of the most vulnerable populations in Ukraine, specifically survivors of or persons highly at-risk of trafficking, exploitation, gender-based violence (GBV), and other forms of abuse. Groups of particular concern include (but are not limited to) women, children, older persons, and persons with disabilities, especially those experiencing hardship. In addition to offering protection services to 240 individuals, IOM is developing the capacities of 40 professionals engaged in providing protection services. Furthermore, IOM and its local partners are organising outreach and awareness-raising activities to inform approximately 800 people about protection risks, available services, and rights, specifically targeting persons most vulnerable to trafficking and other protection threats. IOM is also purchasing and supplying various types of generators to prevent interruptions of essential and lifesaving services.</narrative>
  </description>
